### 🟡 Required for Live Trading

#### 5. Implement Real Trade Execution
This is the **biggest gap** in the codebase. Three locations need work:

**a)** [executor.py `_submit_order()`](file:///d:/GithubLocal/PolyQuant/src/polyquant/execution/executor.py#L158-188) — Currently returns `None` in live mode with a `TODO` comment. Needs to call `PolymarketClient.place_order()`.

**b)** [executor.py `_unwind()`](file:///d:/GithubLocal/PolyQuant/src/polyquant/execution/executor.py#L190-217) — Unwind/reversal logic is a no-op in live mode. Needs real order submission.

**c)** [navigator.py `_execute_opportunity()`](file:///d:/GithubLocal/PolyQuant/src/polyquant/navigator.py#L579) — The Navigator detects opportunities but doesn't yet execute them. Needs to wire up the `TradeExecutor`.

> [!CAUTION]
> The `place_order()` method in `polymarket_client.py` does exist and uses `py-clob-client` SDK, but it calls blocking SDK methods from async code. This needs to be wrapped in `asyncio.to_thread()` or the SDK client needs to be created once and reused.

#### 6. Enable the Rust Signer (Performance)
The Rust `execution_core` crate ([lib.rs](file:///d:/GithubLocal/PolyQuant/src/polyquant/execution_core/src/lib.rs)) is **fully implemented** but **not connected**:
- The import in [auth.py](file:///d:/GithubLocal/PolyQuant/src/polyquant/data/auth.py#L12-18) is commented out
- `RUST_AVAILABLE` is hardcoded to `False`
- The crate needs to be built first: `cd src/polyquant/execution_core && maturin develop`
- Then uncomment the import and remove the hardcoded `False`

This provides **~10-50x faster** EIP-712 signing compared to the Python `eth_account` fallback.

#### 7. Fund a Polygon Wallet
- Need USDC (or USDC.e) on Polygon for trading
- The private key goes in `POLYGON_PRIVATE_KEY`
- Start with **paper mode** (`TRADING_MODE=paper`) before committing real funds

